TYPES.md §5.2, §1: a map item in a record literal is E3320, once: the misplaced item has no expected type, so a literal it holds is not judged again (no E3305).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record R {
  a: Int
}

local let r: R = { a: 1, "k": { b: {} } }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3320]  a/a.canon:7:26
  map items are not allowed in record literals

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
